 on high technology  after an in-depth study the Commission  concluded they were not meeting the  competitive challenge well enough it  stated our ability to compete in world  markets is eroding growth and US  productivity lags far behind that our  foreign competitors real hourly  compensation for our workforce is no  longer improving US leadership and world  trade is declining  finally pre-tax rate of return on assets  invested in manufacturing discourages  investment in this vital core of our  economy one of the commission's primary  recommendations was to create apply and  protect technology innovation Spurs new  industries and revise mature ones  technological advances lead to improve  productivity an essential ingredient of  our standard of living in essence this  recommendation was twofold to create  technology and to improve productivity  how do i define creativity Nobel Prize  winners n yogi provided a good working  definition when he said discovery  consists of looking at the same thing as  everyone else and thinking something  quite different that's a good enough  summary to cover much of what I wish to  comment on the trouble is that  creativity is really a poly poly faceted  discipline trying to describe it in  detail reminds me of the story or the  three blind men who attempted to  describe an elephant solely by their  scent but sense of field one explored  the trunk one discovered the tusks the  third investigated the animals enormous  feat but none really had a good look  good picture of what the old but the  whole animal looked like I would like to  describe my elephant creativity as I've  had it  to desert to observe it over these years  first let me make one general comment  about creative people  education is not a sin KO known for  being creative the Kasich point is that  of the most successful engineer who  worked for us for many years despite the  fact that he had only completed one year  of college he was one of the most  creative people I have known you could  present Larry with the most difficult  problem and he would come up with really  ingenious solutions he had the ability  to isolate the essential essentials of  the problem and tackle it with vigor it  was such a pleasure to talk to them  about his work he just bubbled over with  enthusiasm many of his ideas are still  incorporated in products we are  currently manufacturing it is very  difficult to spot a creative individual  just by looking at a resume  psychologists can't even agree on how to  measure this characteristic let alone  predict who will display establishing an  environment that fosters creativity and  observed those who flourish is probably  the best way of finding this elusive  talent I would like to distinguish  between two different kinds of  creativity one is spontaneous and which  an individual sees a complete and  elegant solution to an interesting  problem there the other I call  creativity on demand in which specific  objectives are established that must be  met both a great deal flexibility and  how the results are to be achieved both  types of successful innovators share our  many traits in common creative people  have an abiding curiosity and an  insatiable desire to learn how and why  things work they take nothing for  granted they are interested in things  around them and tend to stow away bits  and pieces of information in their mind  for future use and they have a great  ability to mobilize their thinking and  experiences for use in solving a new  problem problems however are rarely  solved in the spur of the moment they  must be organized and dissected then key  issue is isolated and  a period of destination then sets in  during which these issues are mulled  over you put them in your mind and  consciously or unconsciously you work at  them at odd hours of day or night even  at work sometimes it is somewhat  analogous they're trying to place a name  on the face of someone that you've met  before often the solutions the problem  comes to you much the same way that you  eventually recall the name there are the  subclass of individuals that not only  have the ability to see things around  them but also to note that what differs  from the norm a good example that Sir  Arthur Fleming who discovered penicillin  his story is familiar to many of you he  noted that when a mold had landed on a  culture disk but the colony the staff  the cocci the colony is adjacent of the  walls were killed many others scientists  may have had the same problem but it  simply passed by in fact Fleming himself  remembered such a previous occurrence  but this time because he became more  interested when I concluded the bowl  must have secreted something that was  toxic to the bacteria and if so that  something might be beneficial in the  treatment of human infection  thus the drug penicillin was born I have  observed the same creative phenomena and  the same questioning minds a number of  times if you use a few years ago a young  British engineer who was working for us  was investigating the characteristics of  a new semiconductor device in all the  tests it performed basically as expected  but Frank noted that there seemed to be  an excess of noise in his measurement he  completed his project but was still  curious he decided to look into the  source of his excess noise with the aid  of a newly developed measuring technique  he discovered that the noise was in fact  a very high order harmonic Train  essentially a lectric analogy of a water  hammer this turn this proved to be a  very important discovery for certain  nanosecond measurements in fact it made  practical the very technology that was  used for then  the intellectual sure intellectual  curiosity is a great source of  creativity an example is that  demonstrated by Nobel Prize winner Louie  Alvarez a longtime member of our board  while visiting Egypt Louie became  interested in the fact that no major  burial chambers have been found in the  periods akarin that began to muse about  how one might determine if such a  chamber did exist  louia was familiar with cosmic rays and  knew they might be suitable for x-raying  the pyramid  careful investigation led into the  conclusion that if he had been asked to  design a proper radiation source for  this purpose it would have been the MU  meson an important component of cosmic  rays that exactly fit the need an added  bonus was the fact that under the  pyramid was a chamber that extended the  full length of the base in which he  could locate his film that is a series  of detectors that can measure the  strength of the MU meson as well as a  directive arrival with these thoughts in  mind he went to the Chancellor of UC  Berkeley who on the basis of Louie's  analysis provided a small amount of  money to carry out the experiment I  mentioned this because it is a good  example of how a little support can  encourage a creative person the study  was not a normal function of a physics  department nor was financing of it easy  it was just a fascinating subject the  Chancellor thought might add to man's  knowledge of the past lui received the  enthusiastic support of the Egyptian  government and the experiment in due  course took place no chamber was  discovered yet the experiment was  successful because Louis was able to  prove beyond doubt but there was no  major chamber in the pyramid another  example is that of an HP scientist who  was a specialist in designing quartz  crystals used for generating extremely  accurate time standards the accuracy of  such reference crystals is very  sensitive to change in temperature and  mechanical force much of the existing  technology used to stabilize these  crystals has to do with minimizing the  effect of these two variables Don took  the opposite view he thought why not use  the intrinsic sensitivity of temperature  as a way to produce a digital  thermometer normally the frequency  change is not a linear function of  temperature but Don devised a technique  to linearize this relationship to about  a tenth degree over a range from minus  40 to 200 degrees centigrade and with a  resolution of about a ten thousandth of  a degree a major advantage advantage of  this technique other than that that are  obvious was that the sensing element to  be located as far as ten thousand feet  a measuring instrument with no loss of  accuracy in a similar fashion he  produced a quartz transducer that  operate at pressures up to 10,000 pounds  per square inch with an accuracy of  about a twenty of a pound per square  inch and a resolution of about a thumb  for BSI this device has been used  extensively in oceanographic studies and  for measuring differential pressures in  oil fields to determine the best pumping  strategy basic I've been talking about  creativity applied to research type  situations now let me turn to the  development phase where creativity is  the in the is the creativity at demand  is the usual mode here creativity's role  is slightly different there is now a  clearly defined objective and the job is  to find a way to meet this goal this is  the type of creativity about which much  has been written primarily because  techniques disseminate and the handset  are well known one book on this subject  I greatly enjoyed was conceptual  blockbusting by James L Adams his title  suggests that we all suffer from mental  blocks that stand in the way of solving  problems at hand  these might be emotional emotional  blocks such as fear of failure  frustration or too much or too little  motivation they may perceptual blocks  such as using incorrect information or  the wrong method or not all your senses  quite often the our cultural blocks  which sometimes can be the hardest  overcome I think this is an area in  which younger people have a tremendous  advantage since as you well know they  have an enduring habit of always  questioning past wisdom and authority  they say to themselves there must be a  better way ninety nine times out of a  hundred they discovered that existing  traditional ways are the best but is  that one percent that counts this is how  progress is made a wonderful example of  the desire to break from the rigid  traditions of the past maybe that of the  French impressionist painters during the  latter part of the nineteenth century  the most important works of these  painters had been excluded from the  salon held in Paris nearly every year  the offices of days Academy des Vosges  are the salaah jury er juries refused  their work because they did not follow  the traditions of the academic schools  finally in 1874 the Impressionists  several of them in their 20s and 30s  banded together to share the cost of  exhibiting their own controversial works  in a series of eight of these  impressions exhibits were held and by  1886 the oppression of school was well  established and recognized but now to  return to the more mundane world of R&amp;D  projects do not always progress at a  steady rate uniform rates sometimes  progress is stymied by very difficult  problems the problem might be overcome  by a clear technical breakthrough but  more often than not it is bypassed with  a compromise solution I like to call a  hot patch if there are too many of these  hot patches you probably will wind up  with a very clumsy solution to the  problem my company is often employed  retired engineers or scientists on a  part-time consulting base one such was  Harold freeze of Bell Telephone  laboratories I am sure that some of the  electrical engineers in the audience are  familiar with his book on antenna design  Harold and his wife would come to  California during the winter months and  spend time in and around Colorado  Harold enjoyed visiting with our  engineers in the laboratories frankly he  didn't know beans about modern  transistor circuitry but he knew how to  think about the development process and  he'd love to work with engineers who  felt they had reached a dead end on a  project he would get them to step back  and view their work as a whole he would  ask what are you really trying to do are  you on the right track or do you feel  you have too many hot patches or are you  really on the wrong track and need to  make it fresh start this can be one of  the toughest decisions a development  engineer they have to make Harold was  just wonderful and is helping young  engineers reach this critical decision  he had a way of making a person see  things in perspective and engineers just  loved him we always tried to encourage  this kind of interact  in our laboratories between generations  because experienced engineers can be  very helpful in the development process  in this exchange of ideas I have often  seen younger researchers learn new ways  to harness the use of their instincts in  practice spontaneous creativity and  normal development process are often  intertwined and may in fact seem to  conflict witness Chuck houses comments  referred to earlier there is a time and  a place for creativity but in the  development process  timing sometimes outweighs innovation it  all comes back to the question of how  often you can change course and still  make forward progress I remember when we  were trying to bring out our first  scientific desktop calculator integrated  circuits for just being introduced and  we had to decide whether the delay the  entry of the project so that you might  use integrated circuits or go ahead and  introduce it with a primitive but proven  read-only memory device we chose the  latter timing was a dominant factor and  not the nicest of the solution I've  talked enough about creative creativity  in the R&amp;D phase now this look at how  creativity can help increase  productivity and improve quality this  challenge is clearly defined by the  finding to the President's Commission we  need the same creative effort in the  production process that we now lavish on  the development phase we must start by  having productivity and quality as  stated objectives of the research and  development program productivity must be  designed under a project not added at a  later date quality cannot be inspected  in there was already a great deal of  technology readily available that can be  used to improve quality and manufacture  ability of a product in many cases  however US industries have not taken  advantage of this knowledge although  much of it originated in the United  States we need new ideas new leadership  in this quest here the universities have  a very real responsibility I don't mean  that they should go back to teaching  Forge foundry and machine shop subject  that I had to take as  as an engineering student but our  universities do need to provide a  theoretical base theoretical base for  quality and efficiency in the  manufacturing process I'm delighted to  learn that this trend is already  underway at this institution but after  all what else would you expect I hope  I've made it clear that creativity will  play a vital and critical role in our  increasingly high-tech society our  company president John Young put it this  way  creativity is the only American  competitive advantage left industry is  going to have to make some dramatic  changes in how it views the importance  of research and development programs and  the necessity of increasing productivity  change never comes easy it is a comfort  there is comfort and safety and  tradition but change must come and  matter how painful or how expensive it  may be from your standpoint this  situation is anything but bleak personal  advancement and me static company or a  static industry can be slow and  difficult change however opens cracks in  those monolithic structures it presents  a period of great opportunity for this  is the time when the best and the most  creative minds we sought out and placed  in positions of key responsibilities in  the high-tech field top leadership was  always looking for good minds high  energy levels and willingness to accept  responsibility in fact our company is so  dependent upon creativity that we are  still emphasizing the recruitment of  engineering graduates even though there  is a freezing hire in effect for the  rest of the company it may turn out at  the present period we'll be looked back  upon as one of unprecedented opportunity  was scientifically minded you are in a  unique position to take advantage of  this situation good luck I wish you  success happiness and great bursts of  creativity and all of your endeavors  you
 

